  "source": "JoyPro curated on the maker's photo (2026-10-12), Virpil's classic \"VPC Constellation ALPHA\" button-map sheet (flat): main drawing of the right grip seen from the front-left (thumb side and face visible, index side to the right), inset (lower right) shows the back with the pinky button and the twist ring; markers sit on the drawn controls, not on the number labels",
  "mappingSource": "the sheet itself (Virpil support \"VPC Constellation ALPHA grip\", https://support.virpil.com/en/support/solutions/articles/47001250811-vpc-constellation-alpha-grip, attachment 47246730846); every leader line was traced from its label to the control; agrees with the catalog's EDCD 33440388.buttonMap numbering",
  "confidence": "high",
  "note": "all 31 buttons and all axes of the catalog match the sheet (classic numbering: 12 red button, 13-17 square hat, 7-11 striped hat, 18-20 index rocker, 21/22 wheel push, 23/24 wheel down/up, 25-29 thumb-side hat, 30 rear button, 31 lever click, S lever, Z twist). No discrepancy. flip trigger labels: 1 has an up arrow and one dot, 2 two dots; both on the same folding lever. The sheet points Z at the twist ring at the grip base in the inset (0.83 0.893); the twist marker sits on the handle. The base is not drawn; the gimbal marker sits on the knurled grip nut.",
